THE CASE AGAINST THE TARGET:
The proposal breaks reinstatement as a derived property. By defining acceptance as the intersection of all fixpoints respecting a total preorder, a node can be excluded from the intersection simply because, under some admissible preorder, one of its defenders is ranked low and a chain of attacks defeats it. In the standard grounded semantics that node would be reinstated once its attacker is refuted; here, the skeptical intersection over orders can leave it suspended across the entire family, so reinstatement no longer holds as a derived property of the intersection.

TARGET:
Generalize the grounded extension to a family of fixpoints indexed by a total preorder on warrants, then define the accepted set as the intersection of all fixpoints that respect the preorder—skeptical over orders. The covering principle is that strengthening is choosing a coarser preorder, never changing the underlying attack graph. Because the family is finite and the intersection is computable by a polynomial number of grounded evaluations, determinism and polynomial cost are preserved. Reinstatement and committed-root validity follow from the intersection being a subset of each admissible fixpoint.